  "about": "Blue Hour's Blender style sheet as data (BACKLOG.md 'Blue Hour: Blender assets' B1). validate.mjs reads it. Bytes are KiB x 1024. extent is the longest side a class may have, in metres; each item's box is the builder's box it replaces, held to 10% per axis. texture is the largest image side in pixels, and 0 means none. clips are the clip names an item must carry, exactly; nodes are the node names the game finds and poses itself, and each must be in the file. ref is the entry a prop was built at (#665), and ref.origin is where the builder's own origin sits in the model's frame, in metres at ref, which props.py checks on every export so the wiring row can put it back (B5). The palette is every colour js/wildlife.js, js/props.js and js/forest.js draw with, named for what wears it.",
